# Tracing process identity (VCP)

Operators must see **who spoke** in every log line. Never invent ad-hoc
targets that blur the portal and the storage helper.

## Required prefixes

| Process / surface | Allowed `tracing` target prefix | Examples |
|-------------------|----------------------------------|----------|
| Portal (`vcp` binary / `vcp::` library UI path) | `vcp:` or `vcp::…` | `vcp`, `vcp::magic_link`, `vcp::storage::client` |
| Storage helper (`vcp-store` binary + helper-owned ops) | `vcp-store:` or `vcp-store::…` | `vcp-store`, `vcp-store::alert` |

Use the **hyphenated** product name `vcp-store` in targets (not
`vcp_store`, not `vcp_storage_*`).

## Forbidden

| Forbidden | Why |
|-----------|-----|
| `vcp_storage_alert` / `vcp_storage_*` | Ambiguous; looks like neither process |
| `vcp_store` (underscore) as a target string | Binary crate name ≠ ops identity; use `vcp-store` |
| Bare custom targets without `vcp` / `vcp-store` | Ops cannot filter by process |
| Helper security ALERTs under default `vcp::storage::…` only | Prefer explicit `vcp-store::alert` |

## How to log

```rust
// Portal (default module path is fine):
tracing::info!("listening");
// -> target vcp / vcp::…

// Helper binary — always set target (crate name is vcp_store):
tracing::info!(target: "vcp-store", path = %listen, "vcp-store listening");

// Helper-owned security / ops alerts (engine, webauthn, …):
tracing::warn!(
    target: "vcp-store::alert",
    cred = %hex,
    "ALERT ctap2_revoke"
);
```

Constants live in `src/storage/mod.rs`:
`STORE_LOG_TARGET` (`"vcp-store"`), `STORE_ALERT_TARGET` (`"vcp-store::alert"`).

## Docs / runbooks

Ops docs must tell operators to grep `vcp-store::alert` (or
`target=vcp-store`), never `vcp_storage_alert`.

